.policy "ruff-d404-docstring-starts-with-this" revision 2
.description "Start a docstring with an imperative verb rather than the word This; a summary phrased as a command reads consistently."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff D404 (pydocstyle): a docstring whose first word is "This": the text up to the first space, with
// everything but Unicode letters and digits removed, is `this` in any case (`This`, `"This"`, `this:`; not
// `Thisé`).
//   """This function adds."""    ← D404
//   """Thisbe is a name."""      not reported
#include "python/docstrings.rr"

.violation D404(at: node) code "D404"
    "Reword this docstring's summary so it does not open with \"This\": start a function's with an imperative verb (`Return the total.`), a class's or module's with what it is."
    suppress ruff "D404"
D404(s) :- doc_checked(s), doc_body(s, b), match("\\s*(?<w>[^ ]*)[\\s\\S]*", b),
    @lower(@replace_all(w, "[^\\p{Alphabetic}\\p{N}]", "")) = "this".